  "published": "2026-11-19T08:46:15Z",
  "modified": "2026-11-19T08:46:15Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak at the XML nesting depth limit\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116154.patch: limit the nesting depth while\n       parsing in ParseOpenTag() and NewXMLTree() and free the whole tree in\n       DestroyXMLTree() in magick/xml-tree.c\n     - CVE-2026-116154\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak of parameter entities\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116155.patch: free the predefined entity values\n       on the success and error returns of ParseInternalDoctype() in\n       magick/xml-tree.c\n     - CVE-2026-116155\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the MSL decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116146.patch: destroy whole image lists instead\n       of their first image in coders/msl.c\n     - CVE-2026-116146\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leaks in PerlMagick\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116157.patch: free the strings returned by\n       InterpretImageProperties() in PerlMagick/quantum/quantum.xs.in\n     - CVE-2026-116157\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: list-length limit bypass in the PS and PDF decoders\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116143.patch: check the requested scene against\n       the list-length resource limit before adding placeholder scenes in\n       coders/ps.c and coders/pdf.c\n     - CVE-2026-116143",
